⚠️ severity: IMPORTANT —
⚠️ **IMPORTANT: `setRoleChain` leaves inherit-default sibling wrappers stale — a runtime switch still silently doesn't take effect for them**

`streamForRole` caches per-role wrappers in `_wrappers` across runs by design (cooldowns/chain position persist), but `setRoleChain` invalidates only the switched role's wrapper (`model_resolver.dart:618`). Roles **not** present in `config.roles` resolve by inheriting the `default` chain — and their cached wrapper, if built *before* the switch, keeps streaming the **pre-switch** chain forever:

```dart
// streamForRole: cached until explicitly removed
return _wrappers.putIfAbsent(role, () { final entries = chainFor(role); ... });
// setRoleChain: only the switched role is invalidated
_wrappers.remove(role);
```

Concrete repro: a minimal config with only `roles.default` set → a compaction run (or stall takeover) builds the `smol` wrapper inheriting claude → `/model gpt-5` on a catalog-default endpoint (no scoped key name, so no `addSecret`/`_seedEnvKeyStack` side effect clears wrappers) → every later compaction summary and smol takeover still streams **claude** while the main agent runs gpt-5. The wrapper invalidation is currently path-dependent: switch paths that seed a scoped key name (`_switchModel`, `/provider` with a saved entry) accidentally clear *all* wrappers via `addSecret`, the plain catalog-default switch clears none.

This is pre-existing behavior, not introduced by this diff — but this PR edits exactly this seam and re-documents the promise it breaks ("the new chain takes effect on the next run", lines 600–603), and it is the same "runtime switch silently not taking effect" family gh-2433 fixes. `setRetryPolicy` already establishes the codebase invariant for this exact situation: wrappers capture constructor-time resolution, so they must be rebuilt when the thing they inherited changes.

Suggested fix (preserves other roles' cooldown state):

```dart
_wrappers.remove(role);
if (role == defaultModelRole) {
  // inherit-default siblings captured the OLD default chain — rebuild them.
  _wrappers.removeWhere((r, _) => !config.roles.containsKey(r));
}
```

plus a test: build a sibling wrapper pre-switch (`resolveRole('smol')` with `smol` unset), `setDefaultChain(...)`, assert the next `resolveRole('smol')` returns the switched model.

# Thread 1 — `lib/src/model_roles/model_resolver.dart:618` — stale inherit-default sibling wrappers

⚠️ **IMPORTANT — fixed** in `8ec6bf1ae6` (`fix(model_roles): a default-chain switch rebuilds inherit-default sibling wrappers`).

`setRoleChain` now rebuilds the inherit-default sibling wrappers when the switched role is `default` — the suggested fix verbatim:

```dart
_wrappers.remove(role);
if (role == defaultModelRole) {
  // Inherit-default siblings captured the OLD default chain — the
  // same invariant setRetryPolicy establishes: wrappers capture
  // resolution at construction, so they must be rebuilt when the
  // thing they inherited changes. Roles with their own chain keep
  // their wrapper (and its cooldown state).
  _wrappers.removeWhere((r, _) => !config.roles.containsKey(r));
}
```

`setDefaultChain` routes through `setRoleChain(defaultModelRole, …)`, so the runtime `/model` path is covered; a switch of a **non-default** role still touches only its own wrapper (the default chain it would inherit from is unchanged). `setRetryPolicy`/`refreshCapabilities` already clear everything.

## Regression tests (TDD — `test/model_roles/model_resolver_test.dart`, both named `gh-2433 review …`)

- **Repro (failed RED before the fix)**: minimal config with only `default` set → `resolveRole('smol')` builds the inheriting wrapper → `setDefaultChain` to a catalog-default endpoint (`gpt-switched`; no scoped key name, so no `addSecret`/`_seedEnvKeyStack` side effect clears wrappers) → the next `resolveRole('smol')` must return `gpt-switched`. Before the fix it still returned `claude-main` — exactly the reviewer repro (every later compaction summary / smol takeover streaming the pre-switch chain).
- **Guard against an over-broad fix**: a smol run first benches `claude-main` into cooldown, then an unrelated non-default switch (`setRoleChain('plan', …)`) runs — `describeRoles()` still renders the smol cooldown annotation, proving the sibling clear is scoped to a default-chain switch and cooldown state survives.

## Verified

- `dart test test/model_roles/model_resolver_test.dart --plain-name "gh-2433 review"` → 2 passed (the repro failed before the fix).
- `dart test test/model_roles` → 419 passed.
- `dart format --set-exit-if-changed` + `dart analyze` on the touched files → clean.

Also rode the lap on the same file: joined the split `[ModelRolesConfig.runtimePinned]` dartdoc reference (digest 🪶) so it renders as a resolved reference.
